      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "There has always been a script for instantiating sound objects on particle collision as well as assets (participle) that do callbacks so you can have sound instances on birth, death, collision and even distance.\n\nUnfortunately they never once gave it a review =(",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-07T16:04:11.695Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When making characters with rifles, throwable knives/swords, robotic meshes, etc, I've been less than happy with the results of placing a fixed sound effect  at a distance from my avatar to replicate the sound of impacts and such. I've seen that it's possible to create a script to create a sound object at the same location as a particle subemission, which would be tremendously helpful!\n\nI realize there would be a problem with people overloading the number of sounds with subemitters, so having a whitelisted script which both generates the new sounds at the subemitter position, while also limiting the number of sounds it can have active at the same time to something like 10, or another safe upper bound, would be great!\n\nIt would allow making avatars with drones which make a clang when they impact a wall, bullets which give a satisfyingly accurate richochet sound location, etc.",
